{"id":"h0-01-f1","title":"How a system design interview works and is scored","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: what the round tests, scoring axes, timeline, round types, interviewer signals, preparation plan. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"what-a-system-design-interview-really-tests","title":"What a system design interview really tests","html":"<p><strong>The interview is not a quiz about one right answer. It is a 45 to 60 minute conversation that shows how you think when the problem is vague.</strong> The interviewer wants to see whether you can take \"design Instagram\" and turn it into requirements, numbers, a sensible architecture and honest trade-offs, while staying calm and collaborative.</p>\n<p>There is no single correct design. Two candidates can draw different boxes and both pass, if each one can defend the choices with numbers and say what breaks.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 896.8 68\" width=\"896.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"What flows through a good interview\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M288.8 34 L344.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M288.8 34 L344.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M434.8 34 L490.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M434.8 34 L490.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M580.8 34 L636.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M580.8 34 L636.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M732.8 34 L788.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M732.8 34 L788.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Vague prompt</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"233.60000000000002\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Requirements</text><rect x=\"344.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"389.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Numbers</text><rect x=\"490.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"535.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Design</text><rect x=\"636.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"684.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Deep dives</text><rect x=\"788.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"836.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Trade-offs</text></svg><figcaption>What flows through a good interview</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Prompt: \"Design a URL shortener.\" A weak start is drawing a database at once. A strong start asks: how many new URLs per day (say 100M), read to write ratio (say 100:1), how long links live (5 years), custom aliases needed? Those four answers give 100M / 86,400 = about 1,160 writes/s, about 116,000 reads/s, and 100M x 365 x 5 = 182B rows. That already says \"this is a read-heavy key-value problem that needs caching and sharding\".</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Big-tech loops (Google, Meta, Amazon, Uber, Stripe, Swiggy) all have a design round for senior engineers. The rubric differs in wording but the shape is the same: scoping, structure, depth, trade-offs, communication.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> It is like an architect meeting a client: you do not start laying bricks, you ask how many people will live there and what the budget is.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Treating it like an exam and hunting for \"the answer\" instead of driving a conversation.</li>\n<li>Starting to draw before asking a single question.</li>\n<li>Memorising the design of one famous system and forcing every prompt into it.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"how-you-are-scored","title":"How you are scored","html":"<p><strong>Most companies score you on a handful of axes, each rated separately, and then combine them.</strong> Typical axes:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Axis</th>\n<th>What a strong signal looks like</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Problem scoping</td>\n<td>Clarifies functional and non-functional requirements, states assumptions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Estimation</td>\n<td>Quick, sensible numbers that steer the design</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Architecture</td>\n<td>Clean components, correct data flow, right storage choices</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Depth</td>\n<td>Goes deep on 1 or 2 hard parts (not shallow on everything)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trade-offs</td>\n<td>Names alternatives, says why chosen, what breaks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Communication</td>\n<td>Structured, checks in, takes hints, writes legibly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Operations</td>\n<td>Monitoring, failure handling, rollout, cost</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 461.20000000000005 316\" width=\"461.20000000000005\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Each axis feeds a hire / no-hire decision\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M129.60000000000002 34 L185.60000000000002 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M129.60000000000002 34 L185.60000000000002 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M129.60000000000002 96 L185.60000000000002 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M129.60000000000002 96 L185.60000000000002 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M129.60000000000002 158 L185.60000000000002 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M129.60000000000002 158 L185.60000000000002 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M129.60000000000002 220 L185.60000000000002 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M129.60000000000002 220 L185.60000000000002 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M129.60000000000002 282 L185.60000000000002 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M129.60000000000002 282 L185.60000000000002 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 158 L331.6 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 158 L331.6 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"70.80000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Scoping</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"70.80000000000001\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Architecture</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"136\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"70.80000000000001\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Depth</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"198\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"70.80000000000001\" y=\"224\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Trade-offs</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"260\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"70.80000000000001\" y=\"286\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Communication</text><rect x=\"185.60000000000002\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"230.60000000000002\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Rating</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"136\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"390.40000000000003\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Hire decision</text></svg><figcaption>Each axis feeds a hire / no-hire decision</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Level matters.</strong> For a 3-year developer moving to senior, the bar is: you own the design end to end, you see the next bottleneck before it appears, and you choose boring technology unless there is a reason. A staff candidate is also expected to talk about org cost, migrations and multi-year evolution.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> The decision here is where you spend your time. Spending 20 of 45 minutes on the API and schema leaves no room for depth, which is the axis that separates senior from mid. This is reversible within the interview: you can say \"let me move on, we can return to this\".</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A figure skating score: technical points for the correct design, presentation points for how you explain it.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Optimising only for a \"correct\" architecture and forgetting that communication is scored on its own.</li>\n<li>Going wide and shallow: ten boxes, no deep dive.</li>\n<li>Ignoring the level: a senior answer without failure modes reads as mid-level.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"the-usual-timeline-of-45-minutes","title":"The usual timeline of 45 minutes","html":"<p><strong>A rough budget keeps you from running out of time on the interesting part.</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span> 0-5   min  Requirements and scope (functional, non-functional)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 5-10  min  Estimation and API / data model</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>10-20  min  High-level design (boxes and arrows, one main flow)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>20-38  min  Deep dives (2 areas the interviewer cares about)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>38-43  min  Bottlenecks, failures, trade-offs, monitoring</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>43-45  min  Summary, questions</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 704 68\" width=\"704\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Time budget, left to right\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M400 34 L456 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M400 34 L456 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M546 34 L602 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M546 34 L602 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Scope</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Estimate</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"352\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">High-level</text><rect x=\"456\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"501\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Deep dive</text><rect x=\"602\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"647\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Wrap up</text></svg><figcaption>Time budget, left to right</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Design a chat app in 45 minutes: 4 min asking (1:1 and group, delivery receipts, 50M DAU), 5 min numbers (50M x 40 messages = 2B messages/day = about 23,000/s avg, 70,000/s peak), 8 min boxes (gateway, chat service, message store, push), then 18 min on the hard parts (ordering, offline delivery, WebSocket fan-out), then 10 min on failures and scale. The deep dive is the largest block.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Interview platforms and prep guides at companies such as Meta and Google describe a similar split, often with the interviewer steering the middle section. Treat the minutes as a guide, not a rule: if the interviewer jumps into a deep dive early, follow.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Planning a road trip: pick destination (scope), check distance and fuel (numbers), choose route (design), then handle the tricky mountain pass (deep dive).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Spending 15 minutes on estimates and never drawing a component.</li>\n<li>Refusing to follow the interviewer's pivot because \"I have not finished my plan\".</li>\n<li>No wrap-up; the last thing the interviewer hears is a half-finished detail.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"types-of-rounds-you-will-meet","title":"Types of rounds you will meet","html":"<p><strong>\"System design\" is a family of rounds.</strong> Knowing which one you are in changes the plan.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>HLD (high-level design):</strong> boxes, data flow, storage, scale. The classic \"design Twitter\".</li>\n<li><strong>LLD / machine coding:</strong> classes, interfaces, patterns, runnable code. \"Design a parking lot.\"</li>\n<li><strong>API design:</strong> endpoints, pagination, idempotency, versioning.</li>\n<li><strong>Deep-dive on your own project:</strong> \"Walk me through the architecture of what you built\". Expect \"why not X?\" at every box.</li>\n<li><strong>Domain-specific:</strong> for you, Android: offline sync, image loading, push, large lists, analytics SDK design.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 358.40000000000003 254\" width=\"358.40000000000003\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One round family, several flavours\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M172.8 127 L228.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M172.8 127 L228.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M172.8 127 L228.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M172.8 127 L228.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M172.8 127 L228.8 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M172.8 127 L228.8 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M172.8 127 L228.8 220\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M172.8 127 L228.8 220\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"105\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"92.4\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">System design round</text><rect x=\"228.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">HLD</text><rect x=\"228.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">LLD</text><rect x=\"228.8\" y=\"136\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">API design</text><rect x=\"228.8\" y=\"198\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"287.6\" y=\"224\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Mobile design</text></svg><figcaption>One round family, several flavours</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> A mobile-flavoured prompt: \"Design the Android client of a photo feed.\" Scope: infinite scroll, offline cache, upload with retry. Numbers: 20 posts per page, thumbnails 30 KB each, so one page is 600 KB on 4G (about 0.1 s of transfer at 50 Mbps plus latency). Design: Paging 3 with a Room cache as single source of truth, WorkManager for uploads. The backend is a smaller part of that round.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Uber and Swiggy often use domain prompts (dispatch, delivery tracking). Stripe leans toward API design and idempotency. Google tends to emphasise scale and data structures.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A driving test has a written part and a road part; both are \"driving\" but need different prep.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Answering a mobile design with only backend boxes.</li>\n<li>Assuming HLD depth in an LLD round (they want classes and code).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"signals-interviewers-write-down","title":"Signals interviewers write down","html":"<p><strong>Interviewers take notes in small concrete phrases.</strong> Knowing them lets you produce them on purpose.</p>\n<p>Positive signals:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\"Asked about read/write ratio before choosing storage.\"</li>\n<li>\"Gave numbers and used them to decide on a cache.\"</li>\n<li>\"Named the failure mode of the queue unprompted.\"</li>\n<li>\"Took a hint and adjusted gracefully.\"</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Negative signals:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\"Chose Kafka without saying why.\"</li>\n<li>\"Could not explain how consistency is kept between cache and DB.\"</li>\n<li>\"Dismissed the interviewer's concern instead of engaging.\"</li>\n<li>\"Silent for long periods.\"</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 759.2 68\" width=\"759.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A decision with a stated reason becomes a positive note\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M407.2 34 L463.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M407.2 34 L463.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M573.6 34 L629.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M573.6 34 L629.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Choice</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Reason</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Alternative</text><rect x=\"463.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"518.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Failure mode</text><rect x=\"629.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"688.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Positive note</text></svg><figcaption>A decision with a stated reason becomes a positive note</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Naming a technology is cheap; defending it is what scores. Each technology pick is a reversible interview decision but represents a potentially one-way door in real life (a database choice is hard to undo). Say that out loud: \"choosing Postgres first, can move to sharding later, but changing the primary key scheme later is painful\".</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> \"I would use Redis for the feed cache: 100M users x 800 posts of 8-byte IDs = 640 GB, too big for one node, so I cluster it (for example 16 nodes of 64 GB) and cache only the active 20% of users, about 130 GB.\"</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Twitter's timeline cache stores lists of tweet IDs per user in Redis, not whole tweets; mentioning that kind of detail is the \"senior signal\".</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A teacher gives marks for showing the working, not only the final answer.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Buzzword lists (Kafka, Redis, Cassandra) with no why.</li>\n<li>Thinking aloud so little that the interviewer cannot give credit.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"how-to-prepare-in-practice","title":"How to prepare in practice","html":"<p><strong>Preparation is mostly pattern recognition plus drilling the framework.</strong> Learn the building blocks (load balancer, cache, queue, shard, replica, CDN), then practise assembling them against 15 to 20 classic prompts.</p>\n<p>A workable plan over four weeks:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Week 1: building blocks and numbers (this track and H1).</li>\n<li>Week 2: storage, caching, messaging deep dives.</li>\n<li>Week 3: ten classic problems, written on paper in 45 minutes each.</li>\n<li>Week 4: mock interviews with a friend; record yourself once.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 643.2 68\" width=\"643.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Learn blocks, then practise assembling them\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M443.2 34 L499.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M443.2 34 L499.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Blocks</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Numbers</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"373.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Classic problems</text><rect x=\"499.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"565.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Mock interviews</text></svg><figcaption>Learn blocks, then practise assembling them</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Ten problems at 45 minutes plus 15 minutes of review is 10 hours, which fits in two weekends. The review step (compare your design to a reference and list what you missed) is where most learning happens.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Public engineering blogs are the best free reference: Uber's and Netflix's tech blogs, Meta's engineering posts, the Kafka and Cassandra papers. Read how real systems made trade-offs rather than only watching walk-throughs.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Learning chess: you study openings (blocks), then play games (mocks), then review your mistakes.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Only watching videos and never drawing on a blank page yourself.</li>\n<li>Memorising designs instead of reasons.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>The round tests structured thinking under ambiguity, not a single right design.</li>\n<li>Scored on scoping, estimation, architecture, depth, trade-offs, communication and operations.</li>\n<li>Budget about 45 minutes: scope, numbers, boxes, deep dives, wrap up. Follow the interviewer's pivots.</li>\n<li>Know the round type: HLD, LLD, API, project deep dive, mobile.</li>\n<li>Every technology pick needs a reason, an alternative and a failure mode.</li>\n<li>Prepare with blocks, numbers, ten or more timed problems and mocks.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}